From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 22:58:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 064/185] segacd: a D: diagnostic and a read lead, both chosen
 at boot

There is one CD-R left, so this disc has to be able to answer questions
it is asked after it is burned.

Hold Down at power-on and EmuTOS runs the calls EmuDesk makes when a
drive icon is double-clicked -- Dfree, Dsetpath, Fsfirst, Fopen, Fread
-- against the disc, forever, printing every return code and the
driver's own counters after each round. 'Disk C will not open its
folder' is not actionable: opening a window is three calls underneath
and EmuDesk shows the same alert for any of them failing, and for none
of them. This turns it into a number. It repeats because the failures
come and go and one sample of an intermittent fault is an anecdote.

Hold Left and reads are commanded two frames before the target rather
than twenty. Two is what the CDBIOS does on this console, measured
three times in the hardware trace. Twenty might be why the decoder
never locks, or it might be load-bearing. The disc can now answer that
rather than me picking one blind on someone else's last disc.

Runtime, not build options, for the same reason: a disc that can only
answer the question I thought of while building it is worth much less
than one that can be asked again.
---
 bios/bios.c   | 98 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------
 bios/segacd.c | 34 +++++++++++++++++-
 bios/segacd.h |  3 ++
 3 files changed, 90 insertions(+), 45 deletions(-)

